The Discord exhibit toolchain, rescued from an untracked working tree

Four files that have been sitting **untracked** in `~/Project/FCCN-ANTIBODY/civic-node`
since **2026-08-30** — sixteen days, existing in exactly one place on one disk, with no
backup and nothing anywhere recording that they exist. Escalation 2812 noticed them
only in passing, while reporting something else.

They are not scratch work. Each one opens with a real design note explaining the
ordering and the tradeoffs, which is not how throwaway scripts are written.

## What they are

- **`bin/discord-export`** (zsh) — pull a channel out of "At Least You Tried" into the
  repo. Reads its token from `~/.config/discord-export-token`, deliberately never from
  the command line, so it stays out of `ps` and out of shell history.
- **`bin/discord-graft`** (python) — fold DiscordChatExporter's per-thread HTML files
  back into their parent page, each thread collapsed under the message that started it.
  Exact rather than heuristic, because a thread's snowflake *is* the id of its opening
  message.
- **`bin/exhibit`** (python) — `build` / `rebuild` / `theme` / `publish`. Caches the raw
  export under `notes/<name>/` and fetches once, so iterating on the CSS costs seconds
  instead of a re-download.
- **`bin/exhibit.css`** — the exhibit's look, applied between sentinels so the whole
  block is replaced wholesale on each `theme` run. Loads after the exporter's own
  stylesheet so plain selectors win without `!important`.

## Verified

Both Python files parse; `discord-export` passes `zsh -n`. Scanned for embedded
credentials before committing — none; the token stays in `~/.config`. Copied byte-for-byte
from the working tree into a worktree cut fresh from `origin/main`, so nothing else rides
along, and the originals are left exactly where they are.

I have **not** run them. They reach out to Discord and write into the site, which is not
something to trigger on someone else's behalf to satisfy a PR.

## Two things for you

**The author's own caveat, carried forward.** `discord-export` says in its header that
exporting with a personal account token is against Discord's ToS. That is the author's
note, not mine, and it is your call — but it should be a decision made on purpose rather
than one that gets tracked by accident. If it should stay out of the repo, close this and
I will note that in 2812 instead of leaving the files to rot untracked.

**Whose are they?** They came from another session's working tree, so they are committed
here under this repo's normal authorship rather than claimed. If you know who wrote them
and want the history to say so, say the word and I will redo it with the right author.

## Not in this PR

The other half of 2812 — `journal/autumn-ryan` pinned 11 commits behind — is a pin bump
and gets its own PR, as `docket/README.md` requires. The three dirty gitlinks
(`.antidote-engine`, `.atlas-engine`, `.journal-engine`) are ordinary drift and clear
with `git submodule update --init --recursive`.

